# 2026-07-30 (domain separation): the accumulator now DOMAIN-SEPARATES leaf and interior hashes —
# leaf = SHA256(0x00 || preimage), interior = SHA256(0x01 || left || right). Previously both were bare
# SHA256 over their operands, and SECURITY.md carried this under "documented, not changed
# (non-exploitable, deliberately deferred to avoid churn/re-prove)". The "non-exploitable" half does
# not survive checking: a UTXO leaf preimage is 57 + |scriptPubKey| bytes, so a 7-byte scriptPubKey
# yields a 64-byte preimage — exactly what an interior node hashes — and the stated barrier (leaf
# preimages open with an uncontrollable txid) is a grinding cost, not a separation, because a txid is
# the hash of a transaction an attacker composes. The accumulator is the one non-Core component and the
# piece named for external audit, so it is the worst place to rest on an argument instead of a property.
# Changed in all three implementations that must agree byte for byte (host oracle, guest Rust Stump,
# and BOTH guest C++ leaf builders); scripts/check-utreexo.sh gates them. EVERY LEAF HASH CHANGES, so
